{{- /*
Homebrew tap-trust store (read when HOMEBREW_REQUIRE_TAP_TRUST is set; see
`brew trust --help`). Declaratively owned by chezmoi: rendered from
.chezmoidata/packages.yaml — `trusted: true` taps and the trusted_formulae
list — the same source that renders the Brewfile's `trusted:` keywords, so
trust drift is reverted on every apply. This replaces the imperative
untrust-reconcile loop that used to live in
run_onchange_after_01_install-brew-packages.

Two brew writers must agree with this file or the store thrashes:
  - `brew bundle cleanup --force` (install-brew-packages) REPLACES the whole
    store with the Brewfile's `trusted:` entries — hence the Brewfile and this
    template render from the same lists.
  - `brew upgrade <user/tap/formula>` records formula trust for that name
    (safe-upgrade --self, daily via io.nettleton.brew-update) — hence those
    formulae are declared in trusted_formulae.
Serialization (key order, 2-space indent, trailing newline) matches brew's
JSON.pretty_generate writer, so a brew write of the same set is byte-identical.

Any OTHER ad-hoc `brew trust` grant is reverted on the next apply — to trust
something durably, declare it in packages.yaml.
*/ -}}
{{- $trusted := list -}}
{{- range .packages.brew.taps -}}
{{- if get . "trusted" }}{{ $trusted = append $trusted .name }}{{ end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $formulae := .packages.brew.trusted_formulae | sortAlpha | uniq -}}
{
  "trustedtaps": [
{{- range $i, $t := $trusted }}
    "{{ $t }}"{{ if lt (add1 $i) (len $trusted) }},{{ end }}
{{- end }}
  ]{{ if $formulae }},
  "trustedformulae": [
{{- range $i, $f := $formulae }}
    "{{ $f }}"{{ if lt (add1 $i) (len $formulae) }},{{ end }}
{{- end }}
  ]{{ end }}
}
